.Dd June 6, 2026
.Dt REBOOTD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rebootd
.Nd reboot and shutdown manager
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a service managed by
.Xr serviced 8
that provides controlled system reboot and shutdown.
It receives a system gate token for
.Dq reboot
from the Oracle and exposes it to authorized clients via the
naming registry as
.Dq org.5bsd.system.reboot .
.Pp
On profiles where the reboot system gate is not claimed
(e.g., desktop and server profiles),
.Nm
starts but has no token.
Processes can reboot directly via
.Xr reboot 2
without going through
.Nm .
.Pp
On the embedded profile, the reboot gate is claimed by the
Oracle and
.Nm
is the only path to reboot or shut down the system.
This allows future policy enforcement such as validating boot
environments before permitting a reboot.
.Sh PROTOCOL
Clients connect via
.Fn service_lookup "org.5bsd.system.reboot"
and exchange messages over the resulting pair fd.
.Pp
All requests use
.Vt struct reboot_req
with the following operation codes:
.Bl -tag -width REBOOT_OP_SHUTDOWN
.It Dv REBOOT_OP_REBOOT Pq 1
Reboot the system.
The
.Fa flags
field may contain
.Dv RB_HALT ,
.Dv RB_POWEROFF ,
or
.Dv RB_REROOT .
Other flags are masked out for safety.
Returns
.Vt struct reboot_reply .
This call does not return on success.
.It Dv REBOOT_OP_SHUTDOWN Pq 2
Perform a clean shutdown
.Pq Dv RB_HALT | RB_POWEROFF .
Returns
.Vt struct reboot_reply .
This call does not return on success.
.It Dv REBOOT_OP_STATUS Pq 3
Query whether a shutdown is already in progress.
Returns
.Vt struct reboot_reply
with status
.Dv REBOOT_STATUS_PENDING
if a shutdown has been initiated, or
.Dv REBOOT_STATUS_OK
otherwise.
.El
.Sh MANIFEST
A typical manifest for
.Nm :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bundle_id = "org.5bsd.systemcontrol";
program = "rebootd";
provides = ["org.5bsd.system.reboot"];
restart = "on-failure";
capabilities {
    system = ["reboot"];
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr oracled 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
